    },
    {
      "block_id": "2605.25036_p22_b11",
      "text": "As mentioned in the main text, our analysis focuses on the Visual Instruction Tuning (VIT) stage rather than the initial\nPre-Training (PT) stage. Figure 10 provides the justification for this focus. It illustrates that after the PT stage, the model\u2019s\ncapabilities are limited to generating short, descriptive captions. Critically, at this stage, the model exhibits only minimal\nlanguage bias. The emergence and growth of this bias primarily occur during the subsequent VIT process, which is why\nour work concentrates on analyzing and mitigating its effects during that phase.\n",
      "bbox": [
        55.08,
        352.27,
        541.79,
        410.12
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
